    "body": "## get_blind_signatures_melt_id returns non-deterministic order\n\nWhen a wallet checks a completed melt quote via GET /v1/melt/quote/bolt11/{id}, the change field contains blind signatures loaded from the promises table without an ORDER BY clause.\n\nAlso, it seems like maybe `get_blinded_messages_melt_id` in crud.py fetches the unsigned blinded messages from DB when reconstructing a quote response. These B_ values are then passed to `_generate_change_promises` which sorts amounts descending and assigns them to the DB-loaded messages. If they come back out of order, the wrong denominations get assigned to the wrong B_ values, producing mismatched signatures at the source. This means even the response from `get_melt_quote` can have wrong pairings.\n\nThe overall issue is that when reading from the db the ordering of outputs is not guaranteed and wallets expect the outputs to be in the same order as the blinded messages sent to the mint.\n\nRelated CDK issue: https://github.com/cashubtc/cdk/issues/1933\n",
